<Style themeId="cmkn0tkkw0opg0i2ftjg46o8d" />
<Image src="https://images.vialoops.com/cms091k4c0d270jzyr9585vs7/cms0hdlb20j9l0jx8frkpazgh.png" width="552" align="center" borderRadius="36" borderWidth="3" borderColor="#bbe4de" paddingTop="6" paddingBottom="6" />
<H1 paddingTop="6" paddingBottom="6" align="center">The new MindSync is here!</H1>
<H1 paddingTop="6" paddingBottom="6" align="center"><Strong>Your whole therapy week now fits on one screen.</Strong></H1>
<Paragraph paddingTop="6">Between sessions, therapy tends to scatter. A to-do sits in one app, a habit you definitely did stays unchecked, and the question you came up with in the shower lives nowhere at all. So we did something about it, and now the part you need is one tap away.</Paragraph>
<Paragraph></Paragraph>
<H2 fontSize="24" paddingTop="6" paddingBottom="12" align="center"><Strong>Here's what's new:</Strong></H2>
<Paragraph blockColor="#ff9f8a" blockBorderRadius="36" paddingTop="6" paddingBottom="6" align="center"><Strong textColor="#113237">Meet Main, your new home screen</Strong></Paragraph>
<Paragraph paddingTop="6" paddingBottom="6">MindSync now opens on Main, a screen of colorful tiles: your next session, your Therapy Agenda (topics for next time), to-dos, habits and Focus Areas (where you rate things like sleep from 1 to 10). Tap a tile to open it.</Paragraph>
<Image src="https://images.vialoops.com/cmbhkwdyy14eeyc0hgckxd10a/cmvhzwfrr29w30j1i3j5lgf6e.jpg" width="552" borderRadius="36" blockBorderRadius="36" paddingTop="6" paddingBottom="6" />
<Paragraph></Paragraph>
<Paragraph blockColor="#ffc88a" blockBorderRadius="36" paddingTop="6" paddingBottom="6" align="center"><Strong textColor="#113237">New before and after therapy cards</Strong></Paragraph>
<Paragraph paddingTop="6" paddingBottom="6">The After therapy card now has a chart, <Strong>Your progress in therapy</Strong>, which appears after three sessions. It reflects your entries (notes, recordings, Focus Area ratings) and doesn't grade your mental health or your therapist. The Before therapy card got clearer: a summary and numbered questions to bring.</Paragraph>
<Image src="https://images.vialoops.com/cmbhkwdyy14eeyc0hgckxd10a/cmvhzwfzn2b4a0j1ralz8enzp.jpg" width="552" borderRadius="36" blockBorderRadius="36" paddingTop="6" paddingBottom="6" />
<Paragraph></Paragraph>
<Paragraph blockColor="#ffefdd" blockBorderRadius="36" paddingTop="6" paddingBottom="6" align="center"><Strong textColor="#113237">Timeline and Workspace, tidied up</Strong></Paragraph>
<Paragraph paddingTop="6" paddingBottom="6">Timeline now puts your cards, notes and summaries in one list, sorted by date, and you can filter by type, like Reflect or weekly summaries. It comes in handy when your therapist asks when something started. Workspace got reshuffled, and the colors got brighter.</Paragraph>
<Paragraph></Paragraph>
<Paragraph blockColor="#DBF0ED" blockBorderRadius="36" paddingTop="6" paddingBottom="6" align="center"><Strong textColor="#113237">Character now grows from your words</Strong></Paragraph>
<Paragraph paddingTop="6" paddingBottom="6">We rebuilt Character around six strengths, like Courage and Insight, which grow from what you write and say, not from opening the app 40 times a day. (We love you, but no.) If Character gets a moment wrong, tap <Strong>Not quite</Strong> and it stops counting.</Paragraph>
<Image src="https://images.vialoops.com/cmbhkwdyy14eeyc0hgckxd10a/cmvhzwg7n2bly0j1jcvj79zph.jpg" width="552" borderRadius="36" blockBorderRadius="36" paddingTop="6" paddingBottom="6" />
<Paragraph></Paragraph>
<Paragraph blockColor="#bbe4de" blockBorderRadius="36" paddingTop="6" paddingBottom="6" align="center"><Strong textColor="#113237">The AI in Reflect got a name</Strong></Paragraph>
<Paragraph paddingTop="6" paddingBottom="6">The AI in Reflect is now called Orca, MindSync's AI therapy assistant for the days between sessions. Orca isn't a therapist and doesn't replace yours. In Settings, the new <Strong>What Orca remembers</Strong> page lets you read every note Orca keeps about you and delete any of them.</Paragraph>
<Image src="https://images.vialoops.com/cmbhkwdyy14eeyc0hgckxd10a/cmvhzwgep2arc0j1s27omc9ea.jpg" width="552" borderRadius="36" blockBorderRadius="36" paddingTop="6" paddingBottom="6" />
<Paragraph></Paragraph>
<Paragraph blockColor="#113237" blockBorderRadius="36" paddingTop="6" paddingBottom="6" align="center"><Strong textColor="#DBF0ED">+ a few smaller things</Strong></Paragraph>
<OrderedList>
  <ListItem paddingTop="6" paddingBottom="6">A blue dot on a tile means something's waiting inside, like an open to-do.</ListItem>
  <ListItem paddingBottom="6">The habits tile shows your last seven days, so you can still check off a day you missed.</ListItem>
  <ListItem paddingBottom="6">You can now reread past Reflect conversations.</ListItem>
</OrderedList>
<Image src="https://images.vialoops.com/cms091k4c0d270jzyr9585vs7/cms3iveg90oqd0i1stzg9g8zj.png" width="552" blockBorderRadius="36" paddingTop="6" paddingBottom="6" />
<Paragraph paddingTop="6" paddingBottom="6" align="center">Update MindSync in the App Store or Google Play, and Main will be the first thing you see.</Paragraph>
<Button href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/mindsync-therapy-journal/id6739644256?ct=email-new-look" bgColor="#ff9f8a" textColor="#113237" borderRadius="36" innerYPadding="10" fontSize="14" align="center" textFormat="9" paddingTop="6" paddingRight="6" paddingBottom="6" paddingLeft="6">UPDATE ON IPHONE</Button>
<Button href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.mindsync.app&amp;referrer=utm_source%3Demail%26utm_medium%3Dnewsletter%26utm_campaign%3Dnew-look" bgColor="#113237" textColor="#ffffff" borderRadius="36" innerYPadding="10" fontSize="14" align="center" textFormat="9" paddingTop="6" paddingRight="6" paddingBottom="6" paddingLeft="6">UPDATE ON ANDROID</Button>
<Paragraph paddingTop="12" paddingBottom="6">Hit reply and tell us which tile you tapped first, and what's confusing or missing. We read the replies, grumpy ones included.</Paragraph>
<Paragraph paddingTop="6" paddingBottom="6" align="center"><Strong>Rate us on Google Play and the App Store. It really helps us do better.</Strong></Paragraph>
